-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Flying Shark
  Publisher   Firebird, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Flying Shark (1987)(Firebird).z80
  MD5         c545645a8688f24428492937125fbfcd

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. The menu's Figure outlines line adds more; see the note. Game
  logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: a white one-pixel outline on figures on a double-buffered
              Layer 2, from the game's own plot parameters; the play area's
              blit at 28 MHz below the picture in its original time; the plot
              pass, with its beeper, at the original clock

  Note        Keys: any key on the loading screen, then on the title 1 or 2
              players, fire to start. Keyboard P fire, L up, Symbol Shift
              down, A left, S right; Kempston and Sinclair joysticks too. The
              original look: the play area is monochrome, so there is no
              colour clash to fix and none is claimed. Planes, tanks and boats
              get lost against the scenery, so each figure has a white one-
              pixel outline on Layer 2; bullets do not. The bitmap, colours,
              sound and game are the original's, and the play area now arrives
              below the picture in one piece. Fits a 1MB Next. Known issues:
              pace in JNext -0.09% to -0.02% over whole runs, slowest 20
              updates +3.28%. Scenery drawn in the map (ground guns) keeps no
              outline. Missing: an Enhanced colour set; natural play to the
              end; 2-player and later levels only partly tested; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity
   3  Infinite bombs

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

