-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Run by script through the real loader on a NextZXOS 26.11 card
              copy; 1.0 not yet played by the owner; published at his request

  Replay      3 scripted recordings (title, name entry, play, bombs, deaths,
              game over, restart; one with an infinite lives test poke): 36045
              frames, 32603 hooks run original and build from one state each:
              every register including R, all 48K RAM, stack too, and every
              port write: IDENTICAL; 7843 Layer 2 pictures, 1268507 pixels,
              against an independent model: IDENTICAL; 14 broken builds
              caught; 384 ABI cases, each hook entered at all 4 CPU speeds,
              both IFF values, 8 R phases; the start-up exact with and without
              NEXLOAD

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: through the real .NEXCLASH loader on a
              private NextZXOS 26.11 card copy, output byte for byte as nxc.py
              makes it, reaching play; 15-minute soak against the original;
              flicker check clean; the overlay published outside the play
              area's rows

  Coverage    Scripted input, no human play: the first levels, bombs, deaths,
              game over, restart, name entry. Not reached: the sea levels and
              bosses of later stages, 2-player, natural completion

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
